# Sets the system clock from a battery-backed RTC as soon as its driver has
# loaded (dtoverlay=i2c-rtc,... in /boot/firmware/config.txt). The Pi has no
# network time in access point mode. hwclock runs as a systemd service rather
# than from RUN+=, because udev's sandbox does not allow setting the clock.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="rtc", KERNEL=="rtc0", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="timelapse-rtc.service"
